## Abstract

Unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) are increasingly being used for delivery, surveillance, and rescue operations, yet their reliability suffers under unpredictable wind. Most path planning methods use Ant Colony Optimization (ACO) and/or Particle Swarm Optimization (PSO) while focusing only on minimizing distance or time and ignore stochastic wind-induced failures. This reduces reliability in real-world scenarios. This paper presents a hybr
